/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-04-03T03:58:36Z","updated_at":"2015-04-03T04:04:41Z","body":"PGAdmin doesn't even give me the option for decimal type. I should have given my system specs as well:\n\nPostgreSQL 9.4.1 on x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, compiled by gcc (Ubuntu 4.9.1-16ubuntu6) 4.9.1, 64-bit (Ubuntu 14.10)\n\nMy best guess is that since postgresql stores money in the database with a dollar sign (e.g. \"$50.00) instead of as a true decimal number that the ORM gets confused or something since it expects a numeric value but gets a string. It's weird that postgresql stores it like that rather than a number with a hundredth place. I'm new to postgresql, but thought I'd pass it a long\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/89154252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"cnizzardini","id":171294,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTI5NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171294?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini","html_url":"https://github.com/cnizzardini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnizzardini/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/u